// spec: 12 Runtime panics; 11 Reflect
// panics: library-kind
// Under ant run, Reflect.valueOf checks only the kind and tag the type's discriminator names,
// never the contents: a wrong element is found where it is used, as a wrong annotation is.
var xs = ["a"]
var d = Reflect.valueOf(type(Array[int]), xs)
println("boxed")
var items = Reflect.items(d)

// expect
// out: boxed
// exit: 1
// err: Reflect.items: string does not belong to int
